<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n30566" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nāvĭgĭum</span></b> ,
		ii, n.
		navigo, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a vessel, a ship, bark, boat</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b> (class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navigia facere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 60, 152</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">navigium dissolutum, vel potius dissipatum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 15, 11, 3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">probum navigium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Ac. 2, 31, 100</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">luculentum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Att. 16, 4, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in eodem velut navigio participem esse
					periculi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					44, 22</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Deucalion navigio montem ascendit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv. 1,
					82</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Transf.</b>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>A float, raft</i> (post-class.), <i><span class="en">Dig. 43, 12, 1, §
			14</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>A sailing, navigation</i> (ante- and post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in omnes navigii dies,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Dig. 45, 1, 122</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">ib. 43, 12, 1</span></i>
			<i>med</i> (but not <i><span class="en">Lucr. 5,
				1006</span></i>; v. Lachm. and Munro ad loc.). </div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
